const rawSourceContent = "Key Takeaways\r\nUnderstanding Women’s Mental Health & Emotional Wellbeing\r\nCommon Mental Health Concerns in Women\r\nStress, Anxiety & Depression\r\nHormonal Changes, PMS & PMDD\r\nPregnancy, Postpartum & Motherhood\r\nMenopause & Healthy Ageing\r\nSelf-Esteem & Body Image\r\nRelationships & Emotional Wellbeing\r\nCareer Pressure & Life Transitions\r\nMind-Body Balance & Sleep Health\r\nSigns Women Should Not Ignore\r\nWomen’s Mental Health Assessment Process\r\nNeuro-Ayurveda Development System\r\nBrain, Gut & Hormonal Wellbeing\r\nPersonalised Emotional Wellbeing Support\r\nFAQs About Women’s Mental Health\r\n\r\nWomen’s Mental Health Care & Emotional Wellbeing Support in India\r\n\r\nSupporting Women's Emotional Wellbeing Through Every Stage of Life\r\n\r\nThe emotions of a woman change as she goes through her life. Adolescence, early adulthood, marriage, motherhood, career development, menopause and healthy ageing are all times when emotional, physical and hormonal changes occur, which can impact on mental health. [1][4]\r\n\r\nSometimes, responsibilities in the family, work, relationships, parenting, hormonal changes and personal expectations are just too much for emotional equilibrium. Sometimes stress and emotional ups and downs are part of life, but when they are ongoing, they warrant an understanding and support and need a proper professional guidance. [1]\r\n\r\nGood mental health is integral to women's health. Affects emotional balance, confidence, relationships, decision making, physical wellbeing and quality of life. Women's mental wellness enables them to cope with the changes of life and engage in healthy relationships with their own and others. [1]\r\n\r\nStress, anxiety and depression, hormonal changes, emotional changes during and after pregnancy, body image concerns, and relationship problems are common issues for many women. These concerns may build-up over time before becoming evident, affecting normal activities, family life or physical wellbeing. [1][2]\r\n\r\nWe at Manovaidya understand that there are many interconnected factors that affect women's mental health such as brain health, hormones, nutrition, sleep, lifestyle, emotional resilience, relationship, and overall physical wellbeing. We don't just want to deal with symptoms, we want to know the full emotional picture of each woman.\r\n\r\nUnder the leadership of a Mental Health Specialist and our Founder, Dr. Ankush Garg, we follow the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System which is a five-pillar system that takes into account a comprehensive evaluation, every step of guidance, and holistic emotional well-being support to enable women to navigate through all stages of their life with greater balance and confidence.\r\n\r\n\r\nWomen's Mental Health Areas We Support\r\n\r\nWomen have different experiences of life and emotional wellbeing can be affected by a range of hormonal, personal, family, social and professional factors. [1]\r\n\r\nOur Women's Mental Health Care includes support for the following:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStress & Anxiety\r\n\r\nAssisting women to comprehend ongoing tension, stress, anxiousness, and emotional strain due to day-to-day duties. [1]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Women's Stress & Anxiety\r\n\r\n\r\nDepression & Low Mood\r\n\r\nSupport for ongoing sadness, emotional isolation, loss of motivation and changes in emotional state. [1]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Women's Depression & Low Mood\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHormonal Wellbeing (PMS & PMDD)\r\n\r\nMaking women aware of the emotional and mood changes that could occur during the menstrual cycle or pre-menstrual period. [1]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Hormonal Wellbeing, PMS & PMDD\r\n\r\n\r\nPregnancy, Postpartum & Motherhood\r\n\r\nPromoting emotional health in pregnancy, postpartum and throughout the childbearing years. [2][3]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Pregnancy, Postpartum & Motherhood\r\n\r\n\r\nSelf-Esteem & Body Image\r\n\r\nTo support the women to develop their self-confidence, positive body image, and emotional strength.\r\n\r\n\r\nLearn More → Self-Esteem & Body Image\r\n\r\n\r\nRelationships & Emotional Wellbeing\r\n\r\nEmotional support for marriage and family skills, parenting and relationships.\r\n\r\nLearn More → RE, Relationships & Emotional Wellbeing\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLife Transitions & Career Pressure\r\n\r\nSupporting women as they navigate career development, work/life balance, shifts in roles and significant life changes. [1]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Life Transitions & Career Pressure\r\n\r\n\r\nMind-Body Balance\r\n\r\nKnowing how emotional wellbeing, physical health, stress, sleep and nutrition and healthy lifestyle habits relate. [1][7]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Mind-Body Balance\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSleep Problems\r\n\r\nAssist with sleeping problems that affect emotions, hormones, energy and health. [1][4]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Sleep Problems\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMenopause & Healthy Ageing\r\n\r\nSupporting women to understand their emotional and hormonal changes related to the perimenopause and menopause and to achieve healthy ageing. [4]\r\n\r\nLearn More → Menopause Support\r\n\r\n\r\nWhy Women's Mental Health Matters\r\n\r\nEmotions are not the only factors affected by Women's Mental Health. [1]\r\n\r\nThe healthy emotional wellbeing helps children to:\r\n\r\nEmotional balance\r\nHealthy relationships\r\nBetter decision-making\r\nPhysical wellbeing\r\nHormonal health\r\nParenting confidence\r\nCareer performance\r\nOverall quality of life\r\n\r\nEmotional wellbeing can vary across the different stages of life, due to hormonal changes, increased responsibilities and life experiences. Early identification of emotional issues can help women get the right support before they start to impact on their functioning and wellbeing in their everyday lives. [1][2][4]\r\n\r\nUnderstanding Women's Mental Health\r\n\r\n\r\nEmotional, hormonal, physical, social and lifestyle factors have an impact on women's mental health. Women go through certain natural transitions during their lives such as menstruation, pregnancy, motherhood, career progression, menopause and age. Each stage has its own changes that may affect emotional health. [1][2][4]\r\n\r\nIt's not uncommon to feel overwhelmed during difficult life situations. If, however, the stress, anxiety, sadness or emotional change continues and is starting to impact on relationships, work, family or functioning then it needs attention and the proper professional guidance to do so. [1]\r\n\r\nBut supporting women's mental health is not just about emotional issues. It's about helping women to be tough and resilient, emotionally balanced, have self-confidence, and to have a good quality of life.\r\n\r\n\r\nCommon Women's Mental Health Concerns\r\n\r\nEach woman's emotional experience is different. Certain women will have emotional shifts in certain periods of their lives, and some women will have continuous emotional issues that need the help of a professional and the customised support provided by the woman. [1]\r\n\r\nStress & Anxiety\r\n\r\nWomen typically have a number of responsibilities, such as family, work, caring and personal commitments.\r\n\r\nSome women may have:\r\n\r\nPersistent worrying\r\nDifficulty relaxing\r\nOverthinking\r\nEmotional overwhelm\r\nIrritability\r\nDifficulty concentrating\r\n\r\nLearning healthy coping strategies can help improve emotional wellbeing.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Women's Stress & Anxiety\r\n\r\n\r\nDepression & Low Mood\r\n\r\nLow energy levels, decreased motivation and emotional isolation may impact life and wellbeing. [1]\r\n\r\nFor some women, they might have:\r\n\r\nLow mood\r\nLoss of interest in activities\r\nFatigue\r\nReduced confidence\r\nSocial withdrawal\r\nDifficulty enjoying everyday life\r\n\r\nPersistent emotional changes should be professionally assessed.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Women's Depression & Low Mood\r\n\r\n\r\nHormonal Changes (PMS & PMDD)\r\n\r\nSome women may experience emotional changes throughout their menstrual cycle. [1]\r\n\r\nSome may experience:\r\n\r\nMood swings\r\nIrritability\r\nEmotional sensitivity\r\nAnxiety\r\nLow mood\r\nFatigue\r\n\r\nIf symptoms become worse or begin to affect the individual's daily functioning, professional evaluation can be helpful.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Hormonal Wellbeing, PMS & PMDD\r\n\r\nPregnancy, Postpartum & Motherhood\r\n\r\nBeing pregnant or a mother can cause major emotional, physical and lifestyle changes. [2][3]\r\n\r\nThere may be various symptoms for some women, such as:\r\n\r\nEmotional ups and downs\r\nAnxiety about childbirth or parenting\r\nEmotional exhaustion\r\nSleep disruption\r\nDifficulty adjusting to new responsibilities\r\n\r\nAwareness of these changes early on enables families to offer appropriate support. [2][3]\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Pregnancy, Postpartum & Motherhood\r\n\r\n\r\nSelf-Esteem & Body Image\r\n\r\nWomen's perceptions of themselves can be affected by physical changes, social expectations and life experiences.\r\n\r\nWomen may have:\r\n\r\nLow confidence\r\nNegative body image\r\nSelf-doubt\r\nMaking comparisons with others\r\nReduced self-worth\r\nA positive sense of self-worth is important for emotional health and resilience.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Self-Esteem & Body Image\r\n\r\n\r\nRelationship & Emotional Wellbeing\r\n\r\nEmotional health throughout the lifespan is affected by relationships.\r\nSome women might experience emotional issues with:\r\n\r\nMarriage\r\nParenting\r\nFamily relationships\r\nFriendships\r\nCommunication difficulties\r\nEmotional conflicts\r\n\r\nGood communication and emotional awareness help to build good relationships.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Relationships & Emotional Wellbeing\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nLife Transitions & Career Pressure\r\n\r\nWomen are faced with various life transitions such as marriage, having children, re-entering work, promotions, caring for older relatives. [1]\r\n\r\nThese changes can be a factor in:\r\n\r\nEmotional stress\r\nWork-life imbalance\r\nDecision fatigue\r\nCareer uncertainty\r\nEmotional exhaustion\r\n\r\nRefraining from alcohol and other addictive substances, women can learn healthy coping mechanisms and adjust to their new responsibilities.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Life Transitions & Career Pressure\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMind-Body Balance\r\n\r\nEmotional wellbeing is linked with physical health. [1][7]\r\n\r\nEmotional stress can affect:\r\n\r\nSleep quality\r\nEnergy levels\r\nHormonal balance\r\nAppetite\r\nDigestion\r\nOverall wellbeing\r\n\r\nPhysical and emotional wellness are supported, promoting long term wellness.\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Mind-Body Balance\r\n\r\n\r\nMenopause & Healthy Ageing\r\n\r\nPerimenopause and menopause are a natural part of the life cycle and can induce physical and emotional changes. [4]\r\n\r\nWomen may have:\r\n\r\nMood fluctuations\r\nSleep disturbances\r\nIrritability\r\nAnxiety\r\nReduced energy\r\nDifficulty adjusting to hormonal changes\r\n\r\nBy understanding these changes, women can take steps to manage this transition more effectively. [4]\r\n\r\n→ Learn More About Menopause Support\r\n\r\n\r\nSigns Women Should Not Ignore\r\n\r\nChanges in emotions are a common occurrence in life but if they persist and interfere with daily functioning, they should not be ignored. [1]\r\n\r\nWomen may benefit from a professional assessment if they experience:\r\n\r\nEmotional Changes\r\n\r\nPersistent sadness\r\nConstant anxiety or worry\r\nFrequent mood swings\r\nEmotional exhaustion\r\nFeeling overwhelmed most days\r\n\r\n\r\nBehavioural Changes\r\n\r\nWithdrawal from family or friends\r\nLoss of interest in favourite activities\r\nDifficulty managing everyday responsibilities\r\nReduced motivation\r\nIncreased emotional sensitivity\r\n\r\n\r\nPhysical Changes\r\n\r\nPoor sleep\r\nConstant fatigue\r\nAppetite changes\r\nFrequent headaches\r\nUnexplained body tension\r\nDigestive discomfort\r\n\r\nIt is also important to check persistent symptoms of physical illness with a trained health care provider.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHormonal & Reproductive Changes\r\n\r\nSevere premenstrual emotional symptoms\r\nEmotional difficulties during pregnancy\r\nPersistent emotional changes after childbirth\r\nEmotional concerns during menopause\r\n\r\n\r\nProfessional assessment helps understand the underlying causes and appropriate support. [2][3][4]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nRelationship & Work Challenges\r\n\r\nFrequent relationship conflicts\r\nDifficulty balancing work and family\r\nFeeling emotionally disconnected\r\nReduced work performance because of emotional stress\r\n\r\nHow Women's Mental Health Affects Everyday Life\r\n\r\nEmotional wellbeing has a significant impact on various areas of a woman's life. [1]\r\n\r\nHealthy mental wellbeing supports:\r\n\r\nBetter emotional balance\r\nStronger relationships\r\nHealthy parenting\r\nGreater confidence\r\nBetter work performance\r\nImproved sleep\r\nPhysical wellbeing\r\nImproved quality of life\r\n\r\nIf emotional issues are not identified, they can slowly impact relationships, family duties, work productivity and well-being. [1]\r\n\r\n\r\nCaring for Emotional Wellbeing Through Every Stage of Life\r\n\r\nThe emotional health of women also varies throughout their lifespan and so does the way they need to take care of themselves. [1][4]\r\n\r\nSupporting mental wellbeing includes:\r\n\r\nMaintaining healthy sleep habits\r\nBalanced nutrition\r\nRegular physical activity\r\nManaging stress effectively\r\nBuilding supportive relationships\r\nMaking time for self-care\r\nSeeking professional guidance when emotional concerns persist\r\n\r\nTaking care of mental health is a component of overall health and wellbeing, and can be a great way to care for oneself while also supporting others. [1]\r\n\r\n\r\nOur Women's Mental Health Assessment Process\r\n\r\n\r\nEach woman's life experiences, history and emotions are different. Hormones, relationships, lifestyle, physical health, work and life changes can all have an impact on mental wellbeing. [1][4]\r\n\r\nAt Manovaidya our focus isn't on a specific symptom or diagnosis, but rather on the whole person.\r\n\r\nWe are creating a formal assessment process to gain insight into your emotional health, lifestyle, hormonal health and overall mental wellness before they can offer you personalized guidance.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 1 – Understanding Your Concerns\r\n\r\nEach consultation starts with an attentive listening of your experience.\r\nWe discuss:\r\n\r\nCurrent emotional concerns\r\nLifestyle and daily routine\r\nSleep patterns\r\nMenstrual and hormonal history (where relevant)\r\nPregnancy or motherhood experiences (where applicable)\r\nFamily and relationship dynamics\r\nWork-life balance\r\nMedical history\r\nPrevious mental health support, if any\r\n\r\nUnderstanding your complete life context helps us build a clearer picture of your emotional wellbeing.\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 2 – Comprehensive Women's Mental Health Assessment\r\n\r\nOur structured assessment considers multiple areas that may influence emotional wellbeing.\r\n\r\nThese include:\r\n\r\nStress and anxiety\r\nMood and emotional health\r\nHormonal wellbeing\r\nSelf-esteem and confidence\r\nSleep quality\r\nLifestyle habits\r\nRelationships\r\nWork-life balance\r\nEmotional resilience\r\nOverall mental wellbeing\r\n\r\nThis holistic view enables strengths, challenges and opportunities for individualised support to be identified.\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 3 – Understanding Your Emotional Wellbeing Profile\r\n\r\nOnce the assessment, we explain our observations clearly and positively.\r\nThis includes:\r\n\r\nEmotional strengths\r\nCurrent challenges\r\nLifestyle and hormonal influences\r\nPractical self-care guidance\r\nPersonalised recommendations\r\nHealthy coping strategies\r\nNext steps for ongoing support\r\n\r\nWe aim to empower all women to have a deeper understanding of emotional wellbeing, along with confidence, resilience and long term mental wellness.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe Neuro-Ayurveda Development System\r\n\r\nWomen's mental health is addressed at Manovaidya, using a five pillar, structured approach: Neuro-Ayurveda Development System, which takes into account emotional, biological, hormonal and lifestyle factors.\r\n\r\nThis is not just about emotional symptoms but it also has a focus on the gut-brain connection, hormone health, behaviour and everyday health and lifestyle and supports emotional health over the long term. [7][8][9]\r\n\r\n1. Brain Nourishment System\r\n\r\nThe healthy brain function supports:\r\n\r\nEmotional regulation\r\nMemory\r\nAttention\r\nDecision-making\r\nMental resilience\r\nCognitive wellbeing\r\n\r\nThis pillar is dedicated to ensuring a healthy brain function as a key component of women's emotional well-being.\r\n\r\n\r\n2. Gut Response System\r\n\r\nThroughout all phases of a woman's health and life, nutrition and digestive health remains to have a significant impact. [7][8][9]\r\n\r\nIn this pillar digestion and gut health is recognised as an important aspect of both physical and emotional wellbeing and healthy eating habits are taken into account. [7][9]\r\n\r\n\r\n3. Neural Network System\r\n\r\nThe brain keeps developing via learning, life experiences and emotional development.\r\nThis pillar concentrates on building up:\r\n\r\nEmotional adaptability\r\nHealthy thinking patterns\r\nLearning\r\nCognitive flexibility\r\nResilience\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n4. Sensory Integration System\r\n\r\nSensory experiences, environmental stressors and lifestyle can affect emotional balance and wellbeing.\r\n\r\nThis pillar takes into account the impact of these experiences on stress, mood, emotional regulation and promoting positive lifestyle changes.\r\n\r\n\r\n5. Behaviour Guidance System\r\n\r\nA person's behaviour may be based on their internal emotional experiences, hormonal fluctuations and life situations.\r\n\r\nThis pillar aims to facilitate the understanding of female emotional patterns, to reinforce coping strategies and to create healthier routine for long-term emotional health.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHow We Support Women\r\n\r\nEach woman's emotional experience can be unique.\r\n\r\nOur support at Manovaidya is tailored to every woman's life stage, emotional health and overall health.\r\n\r\nWe will use:\r\n\r\nWomen's Mental Health Assessment\r\nPersonalised Emotional Wellbeing Guidance\r\nHormonal Wellbeing Education\r\nLifestyle Recommendations\r\nStress Management Strategies\r\nMind-Body Balance Guidance\r\nEmotional Resilience Building\r\nHealthy Routine Planning\r\nProgress Monitoring and Follow-Up\r\n\r\nWe aim to equip women with emotional resilience, build emotional strength and to support them to experience good mental health for life.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhy Women Across India Choose Manovaidya\r\n\r\nDelhi, Noida, Gurgaon, Faridabad, Ghaziabad and all over India women choose Manovaidya due to our compassionate, personalized, and holistic approach for women's mental well being.\r\n\r\nWomen trust us for:\r\n\r\nComprehensive Women's Mental Health Assessments\r\nNeuro-Ayurveda Development System\r\nPersonalised Emotional Wellbeing Guidance\r\nHormonal & Lifestyle-Focused Approach\r\nOnline & In-Clinic Consultations\r\nLong-Term Mental Wellness Support\r\nGuidance by Dr. Ankush Garg\r\n\r\nThe aim is to empower women to know themselves, to confidently manage their emotions and to gain a healthy emotional state at all stages of life.\r\n\r\n\r\nAbout Dr. Ankush Garg\r\n\r\nMental Health Specialist & Founder of Manovaidya\r\n\r\nDr. Ankush Garg is the Founder of Manovaidya and the developer of the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System.\r\n\r\nHis work focuses on helping women understand the relationship between emotional wellbeing, hormonal health, brain function, lifestyle and overall wellness.\r\n\r\nThrough structured assessments, personalised guidance and continuous follow-up, Dr. Ankush Garg supports women experiencing stress, anxiety, hormonal emotional changes, relationship challenges and other mental health concerns while promoting healthy coping skills and long-term wellbeing.\r\n\r\nBased in Delhi NCR, he provides Women's Mental Health consultations for women across India through online and in-clinic appointments.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBook a Women's Mental Health Assessment\r\n\r\nLooking for Compassionate Mental Health Support?\r\n\r\n\r\nIf stress, anxiety, emotional changes, hormonal mood fluctuations, relationship concerns or life transitions are affecting your wellbeing, seeking support early can help you better understand yourself and take positive steps towards emotional balance. [1]\r\n\r\nAt Manovaidya, we provide structured Women's Mental Health Assessments, personalised guidance and holistic emotional wellbeing support through the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System.\r\n\r\nPrioritise Your Mental Wellbeing\r\n\r\nCaring for your mental health is an investment in every part of your life. When emotional wellbeing improves, it positively influences relationships, confidence, physical health, work and overall quality of life. [1]\r\n\r\nWhether you're navigating hormonal changes, motherhood, career pressures, relationship challenges or simply seeking better emotional balance, our team is here to support you with personalised care and practical guidance.\r\n\r\nBook Your Women's Mental Health Assessment Today\r\n\r\n📞 Book Consultation\r\n📞 Talk to Our Team\r\n📞 Schedule Assessment\r\n\r\n\r\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\r\n\r\n\r\n1. What is women's mental health?\r\n\r\nMental health in women is the state of their emotional, psychological and social wellbeing at various stages of their lives. It is affected by emotional events, hormonal shifts, relationships, physical health, life changes and lifestyle. Having good mental health helps with emotional balance, confidence, healthy relationships and overall wellbeing. [1]\r\n\r\n2. Why is women's mental health important?\r\n\r\nMental health impacts a woman's ability to maintain relationships, provide for her family, work, maintain her physical health, be a healthy woman, parent and enjoy her life. Emotional wellbeing is essential to women's lives and enables them to better manage life challenges and stay healthy in the long term. [1]\r\n\r\n3. What are the most common mental health concerns in women?\r\n\r\nStress, anxiety, depression, hormonal mood changes, PMS/PMDD, emotional changes during pregnancy, emotional changes after birth, body image issues and sleep problems are among the common emotional issues women may experience. [1][2][4]\r\n\r\n4. Can hormonal changes affect mental health?\r\n\r\nYes. Some women notice hormonal fluctuations in their mood, emotional health and stress throughout the menstrual cycle, over pregnancy, after giving birth, and during perimenopause and menopause. Emotional shifts that do not go away should be evaluated by a professional. [1][2][4]\r\n\r\n5. What is the difference between PMS and PMDD?\r\n\r\n\r\nPremenstrual Syndrome (PMS) can lead to physical and emotional changes in a woman's body before her period. For some, the emotional symptoms interfere with daily functioning and relationships and they have more severe symptoms that are diagnosed as Premenstrual Dysphoric Disorder (PMDD). If symptoms are ongoing and severe, a health care professional should be consulted to assess them. [1]\r\n\r\n6. Can pregnancy affect emotional wellbeing?\r\n\r\n\r\nYes. Your body, hormones and emotions undergo many changes during pregnancy. Some women are emotionally fragile, feeling a little up and down, whilst others feel low or might suffer from anxiety that persists and needs professional evaluation and help. [2][3]\r\n\r\n\r\n7. What are postpartum emotional changes?\r\n\r\n\r\nMany women undergo emotional changes after childbirth and as they adjust to motherhood. Although mood changes may be temporary, if sadness, anxiety, emotional isolation, or stress in dealing with life becomes chronic, it is best to consult a competent health care professional. [2][3]\r\n\r\n\r\n8. Can menopause affect emotional health?\r\n\r\n\r\nYes. Perimenopause and menopause can cause hormonal shifts which can affect mood, sleep, emotions and well-being. This change is unique to each woman, and any symptoms that last should be assessed by a professional. [4]\r\n\r\n\r\n9. How do I know if I should seek professional mental health support?\r\n\r\nIf emotional problems last for a couple of weeks, affect work, relationships, parenting or daily living, or are hard to handle on your own, it may be a good idea to seek professional advice. Early assessment can be used to identify factors and support as needed. [1]\r\n\r\n10. How can women support their mental wellbeing naturally?\r\n\r\nEmotional wellbeing can be supported through healthy sleep, well-balanced nutrition, regular exercise, stress management, supportive relationships, self-care, mindfulness and maintaining a healthy lifestyle. These measures are taken to enhance overall health, but are not a substitute for professional health care when a mental health issue exists. [1]\r\n\r\n11. What is a women's mental health assessment?\r\n\r\nA women's mental health assessment is a formal assessment of emotional health, stress, mood, lifestyle, sleep, relationships, hormonal history (if applicable) and mental health in general. Assessment to identify strengths, challenges and next steps for personalised support.\r\n\r\n\r\n12. How does Manovaidya support women's mental health?\r\n\r\nAt Manovaidya, we start by trying to understand the emotional wellbeing of all women, instead of just focusing on the symptoms. We support women to understand their emotional wellbeing, hormonal health, lifestyle and mental wellness through structured assessments, personalised guidance and given the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System.\r\n\r\n\r\n13. What is the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System?\r\n\r\nManovaidya's Neuro-Ayurveda Development System is a five pillar system that takes into account Brain Nourishment, Gut Response, Neural Network Development, Sensory Integration and Behaviour Guidance, all in consideration of Women's Emotional Wellbeing. It offers a holistic view and extensive assessment and individual guidance.\r\n\r\n\r\n14. When should I seek urgent mental health support?\r\n\r\nIf you have thoughts of hurting yourself or your baby, don't be able to keep yourself or your baby safe, had an attempt to hurt yourself, hallucinations, extreme confusion, or if you are an immediate threat to yourself or others, seek immediate medical/emergency mental health care. These are not time to ever delay emergency care. [2][3]\r\n\r\n\r\n15. Why should I choose Manovaidya for women's mental health care?\r\n\r\nOur priority at Manovaidya is to comprehend the whole emotional well-being of every woman, using a systematic and thorough evaluation process, personalised advice and the Neuro-Ayurveda Development System. We take a holistic view, looking at emotional health, hormonal wellbeing, lifestyle, family support and long-term emotional wellbeing, so that women can become more resilient and stay emotionally balanced throughout their lives.\r\nReferences\r\n\r\n1. National Institute of Mental Health (NIMH) – Women and Mental Health\r\nhttps://www.nimh.nih.gov/health/topics/women-and-mental-health\r\n2. American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists (ACOG) – Screening and Diagnosis of Mental Health Conditions During Pregnancy and Postpartum\r\nhttps://www.acog.org/clinical/clinical-guidance/clinical-practice-guideline/articles/2023/06/screening-and-diagnosis-of-mental-health-conditions-during-pregnancy-and-postpartum\r\n3. ACOG – Treatment and Management of Mental Health Conditions During Pregnancy and Postpartum\r\nhttps://www.acog.org/clinical/clinical-guidance/clinical-practice-guideline/articles/2023/06/treatment-and-management-of-mental-health-conditions-during-pregnancy-and-postpartum\r\n4. National Institute on Aging (NIA) – Menopause, Mood and Healthy Ageing\r\nhttps://www.nia.nih.gov/health/menopause/what-menopause\r\n5. Central Council for Research in Ayurvedic Sciences (CCRAS) – Ayurveda and Women's Health\r\nhttps://ccras.nic.in/\r\n6. Ministry of AYUSH – Ayurveda Research and Healthcare\r\nhttps://ayush.gov.in/\r\n7. PubMed – Gut-Brain Axis: Role of Microbiome, Hormones and Stress in Mental Health Disorders\r\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39273008/\r\n8. PubMed – Gut Microbiota, Sex Hormones and Mental Health\r\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39710079/\r\n9. PubMed – Gut Microbiome-Targeted Interventions and Women's Mental Health Across Hormonal Life Stages\r\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41302239/\r\n10. PubMed – Menopause, Gut Microbiota and Mood in Middle-Aged and Older Women\r\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38157685/";

